{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386966-questions-about-teleportation-effects-and-about-making-a-specific-antagonist","id":1386966,"title":"Questions about teleportation effects and about making a specific antagonist","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-09T06:28:40-07:00","id":1386966,"title":"Questions about teleportation effects and about making a specific antagonist","content":"Hey Im kinda new on MTA, I've been reading the book recently, but it was something that was always on the radar, and I understand the basics about most concepts just be watching people discussing and talking about the game.<br /> <br /> I've been running a game where each PC is one of the &quot;lesser&quot; creatures of each game, kinfolk, hedge sorcerer, kinain, revenant. etc. My plan was that each session runs like a one-shot game, with the main theme focused in one of the 4 main games. And now it's the time to do the MTA focused game.<br /> <br /> I've been thinking about making it a investigation game, where they have to capture a &quot;serial killer&quot;(she doesn't really kill, but actually skins the victim face while making sure they survive).<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't want the antagonist to be powerful in combat, but more of someone who perform feats using a lot of planning, she teleports into the victim home, sedates the victim, them call a ambulance while making sure the victim stays alive until it arrives.<br /> <br /> <br /> But about this teleportation I have some questions<br /> <br /> 1 - If the mage teleports from a empty house to another empty house, it's coicidental probably, but what if it teleports to the victim house while the victim is there, but in a way that the victim will not notice, can this work? It's possible?<br /> <br /> 2 - It's possible to the mage to teleport the sedative directly into the victim bloostream somehow, and coicidentally? Like, can she pierce the victim with a needle to make it belive she was quickly drugged, and then teleport sedative directly into the bloodstream?<br /> <br /> 3 - If this is possible at all, which spheres are necessary?<br /> <br /> 4 - Since all PCs are supernatural, immune to the mists/delirium, they probably don't count as sleepers. The antagonist can then use such powers in a vulgar way if there is no others sleepers around? Can the antagonist even &quot;feel&quot; this is possible even if she don't know yet the PCs are supernatural?<br /> <br /> 5 - Im thinking about making the atagonist a hollow one, a girl who was a hedge sorcerer but woke and is now plotting a deranged revenge against her former friends. Anyone wish to suggest a better tradition or backstory for this?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","user":"Rucun","date":". 05-09-2020, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T07:25:41-07:00","id":1386969,"title":"","content":"First off I like your story premise, has sort of a 80's teen horror feel to it.<br /> <br /> Anyway,<br /> 1: Teleportation is almost always vulgar. There are a few ways around it mostly being when one expects someone to disappear Ninja style in a cloud of smoke or as such.<br /> <br /> 2. You can totally Teleport meds into the blood stream and in the way you are describing would be one of them coincidental ways to teleport an object in a manner that seems plausible so I'd allow it.<br /> <br /> 3. To teleoport meds inside a person would be Correspondence 4, Life 4, Matter 2. You can ditch Matter if the meds are living bacteria though.<br /> <br /> 4. The players wouldn't count as Sleepers but that doesn't determine if something is vulgar or not. If its unbelievable its unbelievable, regardless if someone sees it or not, thus vulgar. The presence of Sleeper witnesses just makes it go from Vulgar to Vulgar With Witnesses.<br /> <br /> 5. As I said earlier. I think your premise is great \ud83d\udc4d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":".  After thinking about it to teleport something inside someone I had the Spheres wrong. You would be making changes to a Living Patern so Life 4 is needed, which . 05-09-2020, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T09:39:43-07:00","id":1386993,"title":"","content":"The above is pretty much correct. <br /> <br /> If you are going to inject someone anyway and for some reason don't want to be caught with meds, I suggest you just teleport the syringe with meds to yourself with Correspondence 2 and Matter 2. <br /> <br /> Let's see, Maybe the antagonist is a mad verbena that needs to collect enough faces to craft a wonder that will make her fairest of them all? Or maybe a nut job who has fallen in love with a man from a portrait and is collecting parts of the faces of that man's descendants that most resemble that man so that she can recreate his face and stick this face on a man who is in love with her and has no idea what she is doing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T10:36:52-07:00","id":1387012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386966-questions-about-teleportation-effects-and-about-making-a-specific-antagonist?p=1386969#post1386969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off I like your story premise, has sort of a 80's teen horror feel to it.<br /> <br /> Anyway,<br /> 1: Teleportation is almost always vulgar. There are a few ways around it mostly being when one expects someone to disappear Ninja style in a cloud of smoke or as such.<br /> <br /> 2. You can totally Teleport meds into the blood stream and in the way you are describing would be one of them coincidental ways to teleport an object in a manner that seems plausible so I'd allow it.<br /> <br /> 3. To teleoport meds inside a person would be Correspondence 4, Life 4, Matter 2. You can ditch Matter if the meds are living bacteria though.<br /> <br /> 4. The players wouldn't count as Sleepers but that doesn't determine if something is vulgar or not. If its unbelievable its unbelievable, regardless if someone sees it or not, thus vulgar. The presence of Sleeper witnesses just makes it go from Vulgar to Vulgar With Witnesses.<br /> <br /> 5. As I said earlier. I think your premise is great \ud83d\udc4d</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> oh, I need to read more about the vulgar vs vulgar with witness then, I probably got that part wrong. But thanks for the feedback. So, considering she has such spheres, there is any other useful trick that she can do and works with the theme of not being direct combat?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T10:40:26-07:00","id":1387013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386966-questions-about-teleportation-effects-and-about-making-a-specific-antagonist?p=1386993#post1386993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The above is pretty much correct.<br /> <br /> If you are going to inject someone anyway and for some reason don't want to be caught with meds, I suggest you just teleport the syringe with meds to yourself with Correspondence 2 and Matter 2.<br /> <br /> Let's see, Maybe the antagonist is a mad verbena that needs to collect enough faces to craft a wonder that will make her fairest of them all? Or maybe a nut job who has fallen in love with a man from a portrait and is collecting parts of the faces of that man's descendants that most resemble that man so that she can recreate his face and stick this face on a man who is in love with her and has no idea what she is doing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Damm, and I thought my idea was fucked up already <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I was thinking about she being used as teenager by a secret society that trains vulnerable people to be their agents, spies, etc. But she was discarded for being unwilling, survived and now has awakened and is deranged. But Your ideas make the tone really sinister and even more crazy, I like it!<br /> <br /> edit: Oh, by the way, about telepording meds into the victim, it was more about the sense that this way she could use quantities bigger than she could with a single needle, and could even do it if the person escapes and is only pierced by the needle but not injected, it makes it coicidental, so once the victim is piercied there nothing it can do to escape. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","user":"Rucun","date":". 05-09-2020, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T10:52:06-07:00","id":1387014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rucun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386966-questions-about-teleportation-effects-and-about-making-a-specific-antagonist?p=1387012#post1387012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, considering she has such spheres, there is any other useful trick that she can do and works with the theme of not being direct combat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correspondence 3 (4 in M20) let's you create wards that, combined with other spheres, prevents the passage of certain things. So most likely you can ward normal entrances with Correspondence and life so that living things other than the mage can't pass. (This will probably be vulgar though) or maybe with Correspondence and matter prevent the entry of weapons?<br /> <br /> Correspondence 2 let's you view places remotely, which is great for avoiding conflict<br /> <br /> life 3 can get you things like night vision, climbing claws, wings and such","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T11:07:17-07:00","id":1387018,"title":"","content":"The most coincidental way to teleport is probably linking various doorways together, so that you open Door A in Location 1 and on the other side of the doorway is Location 2, and anyone in Location 2 thinks you've come through Door B in Location 2. This may sometimes break suspension of disbelief, but can often come off as &quot;I was just on the other side of Door B the entire time.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}